WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.751
Even when they're axed in spectacularly gory
fashion, a fallen star of The Walking Dead

00:00:04.751 --> 00:00:08.870
gets to walk away with a major feather in
their cap for being on one of TV's most popular

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:09.870
programs.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.670
Here's a look at what's happened to these
killed-off Walking Dead actors since they

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:13.660
departed the show.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.560
Love him or hate him, Jon Bernthal's Shane
Walsh was a very big deal in The Walking Dead's

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:19.759
earliest seasons.

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:23.890
Shortly after his departure from the show,
Bernthal starred in Martin Scorsese's The

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.140
Wolf of Wall Street as Quaalude supplier Brad
Bodnick.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.760
He also landed the leading role in Mob City,
from original Walking Dead showrunner Frank

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.020
Darabont and continued to impress in cinematic
action fare like Fury and Baby Driver.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.000
Apart from his Walking Dead role, though,
Bernthal is perhaps best known for his turn

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.280
as Frank Castle in Marvel's The Punisher for
Netflix.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.980
Sarah Wayne Callies' Lori Grimes was another
divisive but paramount part of The Walking

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:49.989
Dead's initial run.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:53.960
Though she was initially hesitant to take
on another TV role after The Walking Dead,

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.310
she landed a leading role in USA Network's
alien invasion series Colony, which lasted

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.420
for three seasons.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.720
Soon after, she also reprised her most noteworthy
pre-Dead role in Fox's Prison Break revival.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.500
While most of The Walking Dead's deathbound
cast members get a call from the showrunners

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.070
to let them know their characters are being
killed off, it was Jeffrey DeMunn who did

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.710
the dialing about Dale's fate.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.750
The actor had a long working relationship
with Frank Darabont, and said he was "furious"

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.740
about how Darabont had been "pushed out of
the show" after its inaugural season, so he

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.340
quit.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.400
It didn't take long for DeMunn to reconnect
with Darabont.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.960
DeMunn starred as police chief Hal Morrison
in Darabont's short-lived noir series Mob

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:30.560
City.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.600
He's branched out into other TV projects since
then, as well.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.610
After enjoying guest roles on several popular
series, DeMunn became a regular on Showtime's

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.080
Billions as the central character's father,
Chuck Rhoades, Sr.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.020
Laurie Holden was also one of The Walking
Dead's initial cast members who had a prior

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.800
working relationship with Darabont on The
Mist.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.860
But the death of Andrea wasn't as instantaneous
as Dale's.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.250
In fact, she became an important factor in
season 3's war with the Governor, until she

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.380
faced an especially gnarly demise at the hands
of his reawakened henchman.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:03.940
Since her Walking Dead departure, Holden enjoyed
a recurring role on FX's The Americans as

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:09.310
Renee, the new wife of the series' central
FBI agent who, spoilers, may or may not have

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.280
actually been a Russian spy.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.540
She also has a recurring role on Fox's legal
drama Proven Innocent.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:18.920
Unlike most of the earliest characters in
The Walking Dead, Merle Dixon did not first

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.660
come from the comics and was instead an original
creation of the show.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.020
Actor Michael Rooker had never struggled to
secure work before, but things really started

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.760
to take off after The Walking Dead.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:33.340
In fact, he may even be better known for his
work in the MCU as Guardians of the Galaxy's

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.770
Yondu than Merle.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.920
He's also since starred in films like The
Belko Experiment and HBO's third season of

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.920
True Detective.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:44.240
As The Walking Dead's first major antagonist,
the Governor brought a lot of shocking moments

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.060
to the screen.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.460
Since he left The Walking Dead, David Morrissey
has continued to impress on the small screen,

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.920
starting with a regular role as Tobias Shepherd
on the second season of sci-fi series Extant.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.720
Interestingly enough, that allowed him to
work with Jeffrey Dean Morgan, who would later

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.340
become The Walking Dead's mega-villain Negan.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.960
Before he joined the rest of the survivors
as Tyreese Williams, Chad L. Coleman was already

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.720
known for his performance as Dennis "Cutty"
Wise on HBO's The Wire.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.520
Since his time on Dead came to a heartbreaking
end, Coleman has continued to amass impressive

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.670
TV credits.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:19.281
In addition to enjoying recurring roles on
several popular TV shows, Coleman joined the

00:03:19.281 --> 00:03:24.240
cast of The Expanse as Col. Fred Johnson,
who becomes known as "The Butcher of Anderson

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.800
Station" for his ruthless attack on a group
of insurgents.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.480
Coleman also appears as the alien Klyden on
FOX's The Orville.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.780
Poor Bob.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.180
When the survivors sought refuge at Terminus,
it was Bob who was made to pay for that mistake

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.280
more than anyone else.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.930
He was forced to give a pound of flesh, several
pounds, actually, to satisfy the hunger of

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.490
the crazy cannibals who had tricked the group,
but he turned out to be "tainted meat."

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:51.420
In addition to a role on HBO's The Deuce,
actor Lawrence Gilliard Jr., another Wire

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.560
alum, also earned a recurring role in USA
Network's final season of Graceland.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.680
If you don't get a chill thinking back on
Gareth's behavior in The Walking Dead's fourth

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.960
and fifth seasons, you might be as inhumane
as he was.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.360
Since his character's brutal on-screen execution,
Andrew J. West has made some interesting career

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.100
moves.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.600
First, he continued in the vein of villainy
as Damon on Freeform's short-lived horror

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.269
series Dead of Summer, but then he showed
everyone that he could totally play the good

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:20.740
guy by becoming the adult version of Henry
Mills in ABC's final season of Once Upon a

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:21.520
Time.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.160
As divisive as Deanna was for some fans of
The Walking Dead, she eventually wised up

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:29.259
and ceded all her authority in Alexandria
to Rick Grimes.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.380
So, in the end, she definitely did not deserve
what was coming to her in season 6, and her

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.880
death was pretty sad.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.370
Things have been going just swimmingly for
Tovah Feldshuh in real life, though.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.259
The actress has since earned several recurring
roles on new shows, including playing the

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:47.190
President of the United States on CBS' Salvation
and guest-starring as Rachel Bloom's overbearing

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.680
mother on The CW's Crazy Ex-Girlfriend.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.300
After his beloved character Glenn was killed
off in the premiere of season 7, Steven Yeun

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.190
made some big moves to capitalize on his small
screen fame.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.839
First, he appeared in a few movies, including
Netflix's Okja, Sorry to Bother You, and the

00:05:01.839 --> 00:05:04.020
critically-acclaimed Korean film Burning.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.550
His TV cred is only going to increase, too,
as he stars in an episode of Jordan Peele's

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.659
reboot of The Twilight Zone, and he's also
set to perform in another property based on

00:05:12.659 --> 00:05:16.500
the comics of Robert Kirkman, the animated
superhero series Invincible.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.380
Glenn might've run out of luck on the show,
but his real-life counterpart is doing just

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.180
fine.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:26.400
Like Glenn, Abraham and his epic mustache
were both grossly mistreated by Negan's batting

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.820
practice session at the beginning of season
7.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:33.420
Actor Michael Cudlitz journeyed back to Alexandria
to jump behind the lens and direct an episode

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.919
for season 9 and signed on to do so again
for season 10.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:40.620
The long-working actor has also had no trouble
getting jobs that put him in front of the

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:45.120
lens, including guest roles in House of Lies
and Young Sheldon, and a regular role as the

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.520
Cleary family patriarch in ABC's The Kids
Are Alright.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:53.319
Jessie was eaten alive by walkers in Season
6 while experiencing the anguish of watching

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:57.379
her son get devoured right in front of her,
because The Walking Dead simply has no cap

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.180
on cruelty.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:03.119
TV fans are most likely to recognize Alexandra
Breckenridge from NBC's hit drama series This

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.400
Is Us, which introduced her as Kevin Pearson's
long-time love interest Sophie.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:11.760
She's also appeared on American Horror Story:
Coven and leads the cast of Netflix's drama

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.400
series Virgin River.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:18.860
A few months before Sasha's final episode
aired, the news dropped that Sonequa Martin-Green

00:06:18.861 --> 00:06:23.710
had landed the leading role of Michael Burnham
in CBS' Star Trek: Discovery, which made her

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.260
exit from The Walking Dead seem inevitable.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.879
Martin-Green's career shows no signs of slowing,
as Discovery has been renewed for a third

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.900
season, and she's been tapped to star in the
sequel to Space Jam.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.479
Last but not least, let's pour one out for
poor Duane Jones.

00:06:37.479 --> 00:06:41.129
The kiddo only appeared in the very first
episode of The Walking Dead, but his presence

00:06:41.129 --> 00:06:43.980
was pivotal to establishing the mood of the
series.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:48.620
Since the show, actor Adrian Kali Turner has
continued to work steadily in films and TV,

00:06:48.629 --> 00:06:53.779
including appearing in the pilot for Don't
Trust the B—- in Apartment 23 and in Bad

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:55.550
Teacher with Cameron Diaz.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.900
Turner has grown up quite a bit since his
days on The Walking Dead and even recently

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:02.680
shared a photo of himself holding a little
Duane doll for old time's sake.

